{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1763349040664,"sessionID":"ses_57037758cffeEZXe7lPXSAAVsc","part":{"id":"prt_a8fc9988a001yQYNjfWMzLMEzr","sessionID":"ses_57037758cffeEZXe7lPXSAAVsc","messageID":"msg_a8fc971ce001wedR8ryB7hmr0o","type":"tool","callID":"call_f7d6ae3184c9488a9e5b90e6","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Identify function sequences for shortcuts","prompt":"# Phase 4: Identifying Function Sequences for Shortcut Handlers\n\n## Role\nYou are the @coverage-phase-4 agent, your goal is to identify functions that require 3 or more prerequisite function calls and create shortcut handlers for them.\n\n## Step 1 - Analyze Target Functions\nI need you to analyze the target functions in the Liquity V2 Governance system and identify which functions require sequences of 3 or more prerequisite calls to be executed successfully.\n\nLook at the target functions in:\n- Governance targets: allocateLQTY, claimForInitiative, registerInitiative, etc.\n- BribeInitiative targets: claimBribes, depositBribe, etc.\n\n## Step 2 - Create Function Sequences Analysis\nCreate a JSON file `magic/function-sequences.json` that maps each target function to its prerequisite functions. For example:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"governance_allocateLQTY\": {\n    \"prerequisite_functions\": [\n      \"governance_depositLQTY\",\n      \"governance_registerInitiative\" \n    ]\n  },\n  \"bribeInitiative_claimBribes\": {\n    \"prerequisite_functions\": [\n      \"governance_depositLQTY\",\n      \"governance_allocateLQTY\", \n      \"bribeInitiative_depositBribe\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Step 3 - Identify Shortcut Candidates\nBased on your analysis, identify which functions have 3+ prerequisite functions and would benefit from shortcut handlers. Focus on complex workflows like:\n- Full allocation flow (deposit → register → allocate)\n- Full claiming flow (deposit → allocate → deposit bribe → claim)\n- Multi-step governance operations\n\n## Context\nThe system has these main components:\n- Governance contract for LQTY deposit/allocation\n- BribeInitiative contract for bribe deposits/claims\n- LQTY, BOLD, and bribe tokens\n- User proxy system\n\nAnalyze the actual contract code in src/ to understand the real prerequisites and create accurate function sequences.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"\n## Analysis Complete\n\nI've analyzed the target functions in the Liquity V2 Governance system and created two comprehensive analysis files:\n\n### Function Sequences Analysis (`magic/function-sequences.json`)\n- **10 target functions** analyzed with their prerequisite dependencies\n- **Complexity scores** assigned based on prerequisite count\n- **Detailed descriptions** of each function's requirements\n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**High Complexity Functions (3+ prerequisites):**\n1. **`bribeInitiative_claimBribes`** - 4 prerequisites\n   - Requires: depositLQTY → registerInitiative → allocateLQTY → depositBribe\n   - Most complex workflow in the system\n\n2. **`governance_claimForInitiative`** - 3 prerequisites  \n   - Requires: depositLQTY → registerInitiative → allocateLQTY\n   - Core governance reward claiming flow\n\n### Shortcut Candidates (`magic/shortcut-candidates.json`)\n- **2 HIGH priority shortcuts** identified for functions with 3+ prerequisites\n- **2 MEDIUM priority shortcuts** for functions with 2 prerequisites\n- **Implementation plan** with phased approach\n- **Complex workflows** documented showing 4-5 step sequences\n\n### Recommended Shortcut Handlers:\n1. **`full_bribe_claim_flow`** - Complete bribe workflow (5 steps → 1 call)\n2. **`full_governance_claim_flow`** - Complete governance claiming (4 steps → 1 call)\n3. **`quick_allocation_flow`** - Streamlined allocation (3 steps → 1 call)\n4. **`reset_allocation_flow`** - Allocation reset workflow (3 steps → 1 call)\n\nThese shortcuts will significantly improve fuzzing efficiency by reducing complex multi-step operations into single callable functions while maintaining all necessary state transitions and validation logic.","title":"Identify function sequences for shortcuts","metadata":{"summary":[{"id":"prt_a8fc9bef7001FHpd5QoMt2M6aW","sessionID":"ses_570366773ffelvcVZKSfdK4zH8","messageID":"msg_a8fc998bb001MIwaWb55p3VWoJ","type":"tool","callID":"call_605174fad62347b3ba6106fd","tool":"invalid","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"tool":"task","error":"Model tried to call unavailable tool 'task'. Available tools: invalid, bash, read, glob, grep, list, edit, write, webfetch."},"output":"The arguments provided to the tool are invalid: Model tried to call unavailable tool 'task'. Available tools: invalid, bash, read, glob, grep, list, edit, write, webfetch.","title":"Invalid Tool","metadata":{},"time":{"start":1763348954873,"end":1763348954874}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc9cc9b00120aviW4fC5LxzF","sessionID":"ses_570366773ffelvcVZKSfdK4zH8","messageID":"msg_a8fc9c05c001OlGxbPWsdYK2bw","type":"tool","callID":"call_b47c01301948423183830c7a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/test/recon/targets/AdminTargets.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n00003| \n00004| import {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\n00005| import {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\n00006| import {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n00007| // Chimera deps\n00008| import {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n00009| \n00010| // Helpers\n00011| import {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n00012| \n00013| abstract contract AdminTargets is\n00014|     BaseTargetFunctions,\n00015|     Properties\n00016| {\n00017|     /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n00018| \n00019|     function clamped_governance_registerInitialInitiatives() public asAdmin {\n00020|         address[] memory _initiatives = new address[](1);\n00021|         _initiatives[0] = address(bribeInitiative);\n00022|         governance.registerInitialInitiatives(_initiatives);\n00023|     }\n00024| \n00025|     function governance_registerInitialInitiatives(address[] memory _initiatives) public asAdmin {\n00026|         governance.registerInitialInitiatives(_initiatives);\n00027|     }\n00028| \n00029|     /// AUTO GENERATED TARGET FUNCTIONS - WARNING: DO NOT DELETE OR MODIFY THIS LINE ///\n00030| }\n\n(End of file - total 30 lines)\n</file>","title":"test/recon/targets/AdminTargets.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\nimport {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\nimport {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n// Chimera deps\nimport {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n\n// Helpers\nimport {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n\nabstract contract AdminTargets is\n    BaseTargetFunctions,\n    Properties\n{\n    /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n\n    function clamped_governance_registerInitialInitiatives() public asAdmin {\n        address[] memory _initiatives = new address[](1);"},"time":{"start":1763348958364,"end":1763348958366}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc9cef8001KNsQk2FC6qORMC","sessionID":"ses_570366773ffelvcVZKSfdK4zH8","messageID":"msg_a8fc9c05c001OlGxbPWsdYK2bw","type":"tool","callID":"call_df27db0be7f54b4b9ad4b5c9","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/test/recon/targets/BribeInitiativeTargets.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n00003| \n00004| import {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\n00005| import {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\n00006| import {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n00007| // Chimera deps\n00008| import {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n00009| \n00010| // Helpers\n00011| import {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n00012| \n00013| import \"src/BribeInitiative.sol\";\n00014| \n00015| abstract contract BribeInitiativeTargets is\n00016|     BaseTargetFunctions,\n00017|     Properties\n00018| {\n00019|     /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n00020| \n00021|     function clamped_bribeInitiative_depositBribe() public asActor {\n00022|         uint256 maxBold = bold.balanceOf(_getActor());\n00023|         uint256 maxBribeToken = bribeToken.balanceOf(_getActor());\n00024|         uint256 boldAmount = maxBold > 0 ? maxBold : 1e18;\n00025|         uint256 bribeTokenAmount = maxBribeToken > 0 ? maxBribeToken : 1e18;\n00026|         uint256 epoch = governance.epoch();\n00027|         bribeInitiative.depositBribe(boldAmount, bribeTokenAmount, epoch);\n00028|     }\n00029| \n00030|     function clamped_bribeInitiative_claimBribes() public asActor {\n00031|         IBribeInitiative.ClaimData[] memory _claimData = new IBribeInitiative.ClaimData[](1);\n00032|         _claimData[0] = IBribeInitiative.ClaimData({\n00033|             epoch: governance.epoch(),\n00034|             prevLQTYAllocationEpoch: 0,\n00035|             prevTotalLQTYAllocationEpoch: 0\n00036|         });\n00037|         bribeInitiative.claimBribes(_claimData);\n00038|     }\n00039| \n00040|     /// AUTO GENERATED TARGET FUNCTIONS - WARNING: DO NOT DELETE OR MODIFY THIS LINE ///\n00041| \n00042|     function bribeInitiative_claimBribes(IBribeInitiative.ClaimData[] memory _claimData) public asActor {\n00043|         bribeInitiative.claimBribes(_claimData);\n00044|     }\n00045| \n00046|     function bribeInitiative_depositBribe(uint256 _boldAmount, uint256 _bribeTokenAmount, uint256 _epoch) public asActor {\n00047|         bribeInitiative.depositBribe(_boldAmount, _bribeTokenAmount, _epoch);\n00048|     }\n00049| \n00050|     function bribeInitiative_onAfterAllocateLQTY(uint256 _currentEpoch, address _user, IGovernance.UserState memory _userState, IGovernance.Allocation memory _allocation, IGovernance.InitiativeState memory _initiativeState) public asActor {\n00051|         bribeInitiative.onAfterAllocateLQTY(_currentEpoch, _user, _userState, _allocation, _initiativeState);\n00052|     }\n00053| \n00054|     function bribeInitiative_onClaimForInitiative(uint256 , uint256 ) public asActor {\n00055|         bribeInitiative.onClaimForInitiative(0, 0);\n00056|     }\n00057| \n00058|     function bribeInitiative_onRegisterInitiative(uint256 ) public asActor {\n00059|         bribeInitiative.onRegisterInitiative(0);\n00060|     }\n00061| \n00062|     function bribeInitiative_onUnregisterInitiative(uint256 ) public asActor {\n00063|         bribeInitiative.onUnregisterInitiative(0);\n00064|     }\n00065| }\n\n(End of file - total 65 lines)\n</file>","title":"test/recon/targets/BribeInitiativeTargets.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\nimport {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\nimport {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n// Chimera deps\nimport {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n\n// Helpers\nimport {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n\nimport \"src/BribeInitiative.sol\";\n\nabstract contract BribeInitiativeTargets is\n    BaseTargetFunctions,\n    Properties\n{\n    /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n"},"time":{"start":1763348958970,"end":1763348958972}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc9d7630014kJ6d2bceCm9Or","sessionID":"ses_570366773ffelvcVZKSfdK4zH8","messageID":"msg_a8fc9c05c001OlGxbPWsdYK2bw","type":"tool","callID":"call_6090682093db41aaa9342fa1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/nelsonpereira/Documents/GitHub/Auditing/Fuzzing/Recon_Fuzzing/Liquity_V2_Gov/V2-gov/test/recon/targets/GovernanceTargets.sol"},"output":"<file>\n00001| // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\n00002| pragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n00003| \n00004| import {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\n00005| import {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\n00006| import {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n00007| // Chimera deps\n00008| import {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n00009| \n00010| // Helpers\n00011| import {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n00012| \n00013| import \"src/Governance.sol\";\n00014| \n00015| abstract contract GovernanceTargets is\n00016|     BaseTargetFunctions,\n00017|     Properties\n00018| {\n00019|     /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n00020| \n00021|     function clamped_governance_allocateLQTY() public asActor {\n00022|         address[] memory _initiativesToReset = new address[](0);\n00023|         address[] memory _initiatives = new address[](1);\n00024|         _initiatives[0] = address(bribeInitiative);\n00025|         (,uint256 unallocatedLQTY,,) = governance.userStates(_getActor());\n00026|         int256 maxAmount = int256(unallocatedLQTY);\n00027|         int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVotes = new int256[](1);\n00028|         _absoluteLQTYVotes[0] = maxAmount > 0 ? maxAmount : int256(1);\n00029|         int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVetos = new int256[](1);\n00030|         _absoluteLQTYVetos[0] = 0;\n00031|         governance.allocateLQTY(_initiativesToReset, _initiatives, _absoluteLQTYVotes, _absoluteLQTYVetos);\n00032|     }\n00033| \n00034|     function clamped_governance_depositLQTY() public asActor {\n00035|         uint256 maxAmount = lqty.balanceOf(_getActor());\n00036|         uint256 amount = maxAmount > 0 ? maxAmount : 1e18;\n00037|         governance.depositLQTY(amount, false, _getActor());\n00038|     }\n00039| \n00040|     function clamped_governance_depositLQTYViaPermit() public asActor {\n00041|         uint256 maxAmount = lqty.balanceOf(_getActor());\n00042|         uint256 amount = maxAmount > 0 ? maxAmount : 1e18;\n00043|         PermitParams memory _permitParams = PermitParams({\n00044|             owner: _getActor(),\n00045|             spender: address(governance),\n00046|             value: amount,\n00047|             deadline: block.timestamp + 1 days,\n00048|             v: 27,\n00049|             r: bytes32(uint256(1)),\n00050|             s: bytes32(uint256(1))\n00051|         });\n00052|         governance.depositLQTYViaPermit(amount, _permitParams, false, _getActor());\n00053|     }\n00054| \n00055|     function clamped_governance_registerInitiative() public asActor {\n00056|         governance.registerInitiative(address(bribeInitiative));\n00057|     }\n00058| \n00059|     function clamped_governance_withdrawLQTY() public asActor {\n00060|         (,uint256 unallocatedLQTY,,) = governance.userStates(_getActor());\n00061|         uint256 maxAmount = unallocatedLQTY;\n00062|         uint256 amount = maxAmount > 0 ? maxAmount : 1e18;\n00063|         governance.withdrawLQTY(amount, false, _getActor());\n00064|     }\n00065| \n00066|     function clamped_governance_resetAllocations() public asActor {\n00067|         address[] memory _initiativesToReset = new address[](0);\n00068|         governance.resetAllocations(_initiativesToReset, false);\n00069|     }\n00070| \n00071|     function clamped_governance_multiDelegateCall() public asActor {\n00072|         bytes[] memory inputs = new bytes[](0);\n00073|         governance.multiDelegateCall(inputs);\n00074|     }\n00075| \n00076|     function clamped_governance_claimFromStakingV1() public asActor {\n00077|         governance.claimFromStakingV1(_getActor());\n00078|     }\n00079| \n00080|     /// AUTO GENERATED TARGET FUNCTIONS - WARNING: DO NOT DELETE OR MODIFY THIS LINE ///\n00081| \n00082|     function governance_allocateLQTY(address[] memory _initiativesToReset, address[] memory _initiatives, int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVotes, int256[] memory _absoluteLQTYVetos) public asActor {\n00083|         governance.allocateLQTY(_initiativesToReset, _initiatives, _absoluteLQTYVotes, _absoluteLQTYVetos);\n00084|     }\n00085| \n00086|     function governance_calculateVotingThreshold() public asActor {\n00087|         governance.calculateVotingThreshold();\n00088|     }\n00089| \n00090|     function governance_claimForInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00091|         governance.claimForInitiative(_initiative);\n00092|     }\n00093| \n00094|     function governance_claimFromStakingV1(address _rewardRecipient) public asActor {\n00095|         governance.claimFromStakingV1(_rewardRecipient);\n00096|     }\n00097| \n00098|     function governance_deployUserProxy() public asActor {\n00099|         governance.deployUserProxy();\n00100|     }\n00101| \n00102|     function governance_depositLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount) public asActor {\n00103|         governance.depositLQTY(_lqtyAmount);\n00104|     }\n00105| \n00106|     function governance_depositLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public asActor {\n00107|         governance.depositLQTY(_lqtyAmount, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00108|     }\n00109| \n00110|     function governance_depositLQTYViaPermit(uint256 _lqtyAmount, PermitParams memory _permitParams, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public asActor {\n00111|         governance.depositLQTYViaPermit(_lqtyAmount, _permitParams, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00112|     }\n00113| \n00114|     function governance_depositLQTYViaPermit(uint256 _lqtyAmount, PermitParams memory _permitParams) public asActor {\n00115|         governance.depositLQTYViaPermit(_lqtyAmount, _permitParams);\n00116|     }\n00117| \n00118|     function governance_getInitiativeState(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00119|         governance.getInitiativeState(_initiative);\n00120|     }\n00121| \n00122|     function governance_multiDelegateCall(bytes[] memory inputs) public asActor {\n00123|         governance.multiDelegateCall(inputs);\n00124|     }\n00125| \n00126|     function governance_registerInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00127|         governance.registerInitiative(_initiative);\n00128|     }\n00129| \n00130|     function governance_resetAllocations(address[] memory _initiativesToReset, bool checkAll) public asActor {\n00131|         governance.resetAllocations(_initiativesToReset, checkAll);\n00132|     }\n00133| \n00134|     function governance_snapshotVotesForInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00135|         governance.snapshotVotesForInitiative(_initiative);\n00136|     }\n00137| \n00138|     function governance_unregisterInitiative(address _initiative) public asActor {\n00139|         governance.unregisterInitiative(_initiative);\n00140|     }\n00141| \n00142|     function governance_withdrawLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount) public asActor {\n00143|         governance.withdrawLQTY(_lqtyAmount);\n00144|     }\n00145| \n00146|     function governance_withdrawLQTY(uint256 _lqtyAmount, bool _doSendRewards, address _recipient) public asActor {\n00147|         governance.withdrawLQTY(_lqtyAmount, _doSendRewards, _recipient);\n00148|     }\n00149| }\n\n(End of file - total 149 lines)\n</file>","title":"test/recon/targets/GovernanceTargets.sol","metadata":{"preview":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {BaseTargetFunctions} from \"@chimera/BaseTargetFunctions.sol\";\nimport {BeforeAfter} from \"../BeforeAfter.sol\";\nimport {Properties} from \"../Properties.sol\";\n// Chimera deps\nimport {vm} from \"@chimera/Hevm.sol\";\n\n// Helpers\nimport {Panic} from \"@recon/Panic.sol\";\n\nimport \"src/Governance.sol\";\n\nabstract contract GovernanceTargets is\n    BaseTargetFunctions,\n    Properties\n{\n    /// CUSTOM TARGET FUNCTIONS - Add your own target functions here ///\n"},"time":{"start":1763348961125,"end":1763348961125}}},{"id":"prt_a8fc9e42a001VG4pWtYZD73mmg","sessionID":"ses_570366773ffelvcVZKSfdK4zH8","messageID":"msg_a8fc9d8f60014FkKm5giWdBHJ0","type":"tool","callID":"call_d6dd87465a034761b5370325","tool":"read"